WEBVTT

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:05.270
The Twin Crown horse girl is now making 
her presence felt at the Osaka Hai!

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.090
In the second bracket, #2, 
the most anticipated competitor...

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:09.980
Tokai Teio!

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:13.990
<i>This feeling...</i>

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.010
<i>Welcome back, Teio.</i>

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:22.680
<i>Teio...</i>

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.880
<i>If I race on her terms, 
I don't stand a chance.</i>

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.790
<i>I need to run so that she's 
never able to catch up.</i>

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:30.630
Ikuno Dictus!

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:34.300
Since your name's so long, can 
we just call cheer for "Ikuno"?

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.720
Wouldn't "Dictus" make more sense?

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.480
Why don't we mix it up and go with Ikutus?

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:39.320
I like that!

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:40.220
Ikutus!

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.180
Ikutus!

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.430
I <i>do not care</i>.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.650
And McQueen shocks us all 
by coming in second place!

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:51.880
<b>Daitaku Helios</b>

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:55.050
<i>I was able to beat Mejiro McQueen.</i>

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.110
<i>I can beat Tokai Teio, too!</i>

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:58.940
You better get psyched for this, Teio!

00:00:58.940 --> 00:00:59.360
Yeah!

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.040
It's been about ten months. How's it feel 
to be on the turf again after so long?

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.870
It feels really great!

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:06.040
I can't wait to get started!

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.280
I guess we don't need to worry, then.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.370
I'm gonna be running against 
McQueen in the Tennoushou,

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.380
so I can't lose in a race like this!

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.220
Then, by all means, show me how you run, Teio.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:20.080
Yeah! I'm gonna head out, then!

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:45.660
<b>Umamusume</b>

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:45.660
<b><i>Pretty Derby</i></b>

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:57.550
Episode 4
\hTM Showdown!

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.520
Teio!

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.520
Go!

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.360
Ikuno Dictus is currently leading the pack,

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.530
keeping a good distance ahead!

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.680
Ikuno Dictus!

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:01.910
What happened to the name 
you just came up with?

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:04.370
<i>I want to get further away, but...</i>

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.300
Teio!

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.490
She seems to be having a really 
smooth race out there.

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:13.330
Seriously.

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:18.360
<i>I don't want to lose! Just a little more!</i>

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:22.470
Tokai Teio is in third place and holding!
 She hasn't made her move yet!

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.220
Tokai Teio is biding her time!

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.140
Forget about the 
runners in front of her!

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.500
Okay.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.990
<i>Tokai Teio!</i>

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:38.200
Here we go, ladies and gentlemen!

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.150
Tokai Teio is moving up on the outside!

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:43.160
She's entered her spurt down 
the final straightaway!

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.660
<i>My legs feel so light.</i>

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.280
<i>Yeah, I can win this!</i>

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.290
<i>Please, stop making this look so easy!</i>

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:52.250
And Tokai moves into the lead with ease!

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.110
She's leaving all the others behind!

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:57.170
Go!

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.670
Is she...

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.760
Tokai Teio is running uncontested!

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.140
The Tennoushou is shaping up 
to be an incredible race!

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:07.800
And Tokai Teio has cleared 
the goal like it was nothing!

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.810
She's back! Tokai Teio has truly returned!

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.610
Teio-san looked like she had 
plenty of effort to spare!

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:20.960
She's not even a little tired!

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.630
And she still dominated...

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:23.700
That's totally nuts!

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:25.510
What could be...

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:35.090
Excuse me, but isn't she faster 
than she was before her injury?

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:38.210
Hosoe-san, this makes the Tennoushou 
that much more exciting, doesn't it?

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.180
She'll be going up against Mejiro McQueen,

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.960
who's got a ton of momentum right now.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:49.280
She's...

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.060
On a totally different level!

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.310
<b>UMA SPORTS
THE LEGEND OF TEIO THE UNDEFEATED</b>

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.310
Y-You've got a point...

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.190
Tokai
Teio
returns
to
the
turf
in
new
racing
gear

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.190
<b>A win overwhelming enough to frustrate all competitors!</b>

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.190
Sure seems that way.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.750
Her knees and ankles are so 
remarkably flexible and springy

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:00.380
that it gives her excessive amounts 
of accelerative potential!

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.280
She's not bad.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.380
<i>She won the Osaka Hai without much trouble.</i>

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.990
<b>TENNOUSHOU (SPRING)
MAJOR SPECULATION\h\h\h</b>

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.990
<b>TOKAI TEIO</b>

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.990
<b>MEJIRO MCQUEEN</b>

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:06.540
<i>And in the Spring Tennoushou,</i>

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:07.990
<i>we're looking at the undefeated Tokai Teio</i>

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.360
<i>versus Mejiro McQueen, who will 
be looking for a repeat win.</i>

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.400
A clash like this is something 
anyone would be excited for.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:15.680
Oh, wow! There've been specials 
about it all morning.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:17.790
Really makes you feel like 
it's all about those two.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:21.300
Yeah!

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.050
Could you please not stare?

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:31.330
Before the Tennoushou is next 
week's Satsukishou, right?

