n
!</b>

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:51.270
<b>C
a
n
o
p
u
s
!</b>

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:58.140
When it comes to Teio, everyone 
knows the Teio Step, right?

00:09:55.150 --> 00:10:06.330
<b>Strategy Meeting</b>

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:00.690
There's a chance that it's 
an exercise for boosting the

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:02.360
flexibility of her knees and ankles.

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:04.030
You really think so?

00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:06.330
The Teio Step is easy, anyway!

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:06.990
Hup!

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:12.090
All right, here I go!

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:13.510
It's just like this...

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:20.450
Everyone, what's all the noise...

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:23.720
What happened to you?!

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.750
Ow, ow, ow...

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:28.770
I swear, we're gonna take Spica down...

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:41.260
The Spring Tennoushou is 3,200 meters.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:43.780
You've never run a race that long before.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:46.750
So you need the endurance to 
handle the extra distance!

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:56.380
<b>Heavy</b>

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:00.760
So heavy!

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.720
What the hell's this horseshoe made of? Lead?

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:06.220
Those were the orders from Trainer-san.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:08.440
It's when you're feeling
worn out that you need

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:10.230
to bring your knees up and 
take a big step forward.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:13.190
And to do that, you need hindquarters 
that can stand up to fatigue!

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:17.190
Teio's greatest weapon is her explosive 
power during the final straight.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:20.010
I need to create hindquarters that 
are able to compete with hers.

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:25.220
That's really something!

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:33.580
What's up, McQueen?

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.420
What? You need something?

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:40.010
<b>Umamusume</b>

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:40.010
<b><i>Pretty Derby</i></b>

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:39.560
Seriously, what are you looking at, huh?

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:43.510
<i>Today is the first race of the 
Triple Crown Classics, the Satsukishou.</i>

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:45.760
<i>All eyes are focused on Mihono Bourbon.</i>

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:48.720
<i>She will be entering the 
Satsukishou undefeated,</i>

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:50.760
<i>just like last year's winner, Tokai Teio.</i>

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.490
I say we start with cheese tapioca.

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:29.150
And then salmon roe tapioca.

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:31.060
I want carrot tapioca!

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:33.080
Teio-san!

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:34.100
Okay...

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.160
Would you like to join us, Teio-san?

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:37.110
Yeah, let's hang out.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.610
Can't. Not dressed for it.

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:43.440
Well, the Tennoushou is next week.

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:46.490
McQueen-san...

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:49.370
McQueen, you want in on this tapi...o...ca?

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.810
Makes sense.

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:55.800
I'm not going out anymore.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:59.320
Two of our teammates are giving 
up their days off to train.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:01.420
I can't just sip on bubble tea 
like nothing's going on.

00:13:02.530 --> 00:13:03.630
Good point.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:07.470
Yeah. Let's help them with their training!

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:16.060
Today's star competitor is going to be 
running in the Satsukishou undefeated.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:18.120
And here's Mihono Bourbon!

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:42.160
This is brutal!

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:44.560
You've been running up this hill every day?!

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:46.880
Sure have! Trainer's orders.

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:50.580
You've never run a 3,200 meter 
race before, have you, Vodka?

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:52.880
Hell no! You haven't either, right, Scarlet?

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:53.930
Of course not!

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:56.730
I have no idea how you'd pace yourself!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:59.980
But McQueen won the Tennoushou last year.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:03.620
And the Hanshin Daishoten, 
which is 3,000 meters.

00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:09.280
H-Hey, wait up!

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:14.820
Seriously, don't land on me!

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:17.340
If you land on me with those horseshoes,
you'll gouge my back out!

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:18.450
It's fine.

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:19.080
How, exactly?!

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.640
Here we go.

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:22.120
Ready, and...

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:28.630
Wow! I'm amazed you can jump 
in such heavy horseshoes!

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:30.590
This is terrifying! 
Do you really need me?!

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:33.770
<i>Teio has never lost.</i>

00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:36.520
<i>If it helps me defeat an undefeated horse girl,</i>

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:37.480
<i>then this is a small price.</i>

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:39.230
Hey, the donut truck!

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:42.370
Oh, my.

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:44.570
Are you okay, Gold Ship-san?!

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.150
Ready, and...

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:48.610
Machikane Tannhäuser!

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:59.090
Her name's kinda long, huh?

00:14:59.090 --> 00:15:00.650
Perhaps just "Tannhäuser."

00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:02.250
No! What about "Machitan"?

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:04.120
We could just call her "Macchy."

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:05.680
<i>Does it matter?</i>

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:06.760
Nah, I like mine, it sounds 
like a world champ!

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:18.960
Keep up... Keep up...
Keep up... Keep up...

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.140
<i>Mihono Bourbon's strength is 
thought to be short distances,</i>

00:15:26.140 --> 00:15:29.030
<i>but going into this race, she's been 
undertaking intensive slope training.</i>

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:33.470
<i>Her trainer Kuronuma's philosophy 
is that speed is a natural gift,</i>

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:35.660
<i>while stamina can be compensated 
for with training.</i>

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:37.290
Is that so?

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:40.660
<i>It sounds like she'll be heading into the 
Classics ready to tear up those hills!</i>

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:44.920
Mihono Bourbon, huh? Seems like stronger 
and stronger horse girls keep showing up.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.200
<i>Will she be able to follow in the 
footsteps of Tokai Teio</i>

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:49.700
<i>and take the Satsukishou while undefeated?</i>

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:51.680
They're talking about you, Teio!

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:55.430
I was really sure that I was 
gonna win the Satsukishou!

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:57.560
What about this time, then?

00:15:57.800 --> 00:15:58.760
This time?

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:03.440
<i>The gate is open and the race has begun. 
Mihono Bourbon's off to a good start.</i>

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:05.940
Huh, that's a nice start.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:09.470
Mihono Bourbon has never lost before, either.

00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:11.570
She's just like Teio-san!

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:15.070
I wonder if that adds to the pressure.

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:19.080
Mihono Bourbon is out in front 
of 16 other horse girls!

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:22.540
Will she remain in first place all the 
way through to the end of the race?

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:27.090
I didn't know Bourbon-chan was this fast!

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:31.340
There's definitely some pressure.

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.820
I didn't know you ever felt pressure.

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:35.070
It's surprising.

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:39.340
But I think a race without 
 pressure wouldn't be any fun.

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:44.350
I think I feel more pressure about the 
Tennoushou than I did about the Derby.

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:47.860
Which is why I'm looking 
forward to it more, too!

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:58.140
You already won last time, McQueen-san, 
so I doubt you feel much pressure at all.

00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:01.550
Teio wasn't running in 
the Tennoushou when I won.

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:07.330
She is without a doubt a better racer 
than any other that I've faced before.

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:09.820
Which definitely is a source of pressure,

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:12.320
but getting melodramatic 
about it serves no purpose.

00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:15.180
You're pretty tough, McQueen.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:16.090
Really!

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:17.260
<i>Less than 200 meters to go!</i>

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:18.880
<i>The gap has grown from two lengths to three!</i>

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:20.650
<i>Mihono Bourbon is in the lead!</i>

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:22.940
She is looking seriously, incredibly strong!

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:26.690
Mihono Bourbon manages to outrun 
them all and cross the goal!

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:29.840
She takes the Satsukishou while undefeated!

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.770
Machikane Tannhäuser...

00:17:39.770 --> 00:17:41.200
What happened to the other names?

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:47.620
Damn, Mihono Bourbon!

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.510
You can compensate for 
stamina with training...

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:57.060
Okay, break's over! One more time!

00:17:57.060 --> 00:17:58.680
You're not done yet?!

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:00.390
H-Hang on!

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:03.850
Now, Gold Ship, 
place your hands on your knees.

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:07.600
You sure about this? 
It's even higher than before!

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:10.330
This would be no problem 
at all with Teio's knees.

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:11.750
One hundred reps, let's begin.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.570
Teio...

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.970
Not a damn word, Spe! I swear!

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:19.610
You'll distract McQueen!

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:21.650
She's not even there?!

00:18:21.650 --> 00:18:22.490
You two!

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.080
Would you like some donuts?!

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:26.090
Oh, my.

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:28.290
Are you okay, Gold Ship-san?!

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:31.930
<i>Are you aiming for the undefeated Triple Crown
 that Tokai Teio was unable to achieve?</i>

00:18:31.930 --> 00:18:35.170
Yes. Those are Master's orders, 
and I will carry them out.

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:36.920
Now, one more time!

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:44.060
<b>Tennoushou
(Spring)</b>

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:44.060
<b>Press
Conference</b>

00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:44.680
This weekend is the long-awaited 
Spring Tennoushou.

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:48.690
First, Tokai Teio-san, this is going 
to be the first TM race ever,

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:50.170
and all of Japan is excited.

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:52.690
<i>A TM race? Not an MT?</i>

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:52.270
Do you have any comments 
heading into the race?

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:54.820
<i>Are they favoring Teio?</i>

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:57.380
Well, I've never lost before!

00:18:57.380 --> 00:18:59.950
And that's not gonna change, 
even against McQueen!

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:04.480
Mejiro McQueen-san, you won the 
Spring Tennoushou last year.

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:06.080
What are your chances this year?

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:07.560
More than sufficient.

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:09.080
I have no intention of losing to Teio.

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:12.140
I'm ready to run to the ends of the earth!

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:14.960
Then I'll simply run to the heavens!

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:17.540
<i>I'm definitely gonna win!</i>

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:17.540
<i>I shall be the winner!</i>

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:19.340
<i>I assure you all, I'll win!</i>

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:20.730
<i>I'm telling you, it's me!</i>

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:20.730
<i>Just watch!</i>

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:28.600
<b>T VS M: RACE OF THE MILLENNIUM
</b><i>IT'S FINALLY HAPPENING!

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:29.590
<i>Are we looking at the first ever 
undefeated winner of the Tennoushou?</i>

00:19:29.590 --> 00:19:32.300
<i>And does the crowd favor Tokai Teio?</i>

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.600
<b>Tennoushou (Spring)</b>

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.600
The Undefeated
 Tokai Teio

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.600
Reigning Champ
 Mejiro McQueen

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:34.260
<i>Anticipation is rising all over the country!</i>

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:34.940
<b>Tennoushou (Spring)</b>

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:37.610
<i>The match of the millennium 
is drawing ever closer!</i>

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.520
<b>Tennoushou (Spring)</b>

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.520
The Undefeated
 Tokai Teio

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.520
Reigning Champ
Mejiro McQueen

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:49.080
Wha?!

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:50.910
<b>THE UNDEFEATED HORSE GIRL
TOKAI TEIO</b>

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.080
<b>Uma Sports
TOKAI TEIO</b>

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.080
<b>THE HORSE GIRL WHO
 WOULD BE THE
UNDEFEATED
 TENNOUSHOU WINNER</b>

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.080
<b>RUNNING TO THE ENDS OF THE EARTH!!!</b>

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:07.890
Good work, Teio.

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:10.770
Prez!

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:17.860
I see. Your trainer's orders, then?

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:22.280
I've never been in a race longer 
than 2,400 meters, after all.

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:25.360
It's true. The distance is 
an advantage for McQueen.

00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:27.390
Yeah. But...

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:30.500
I've just never been in a long race before.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:33.460
We don't know if I'm any good at it or not.

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:35.600
True.

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:39.740
The TV and papers seem to 
think I've got the edge,

00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:42.630
but I'm thinking of myself as 
the challenger in this race.

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:46.090
Mihono Bourbon proved it, after all.

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:49.230
The limits of stamina can be 
overcome through training!

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:50.970
That's the spirit.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:54.550
I wasn't able to become an undefeated 
Triple Crown horse girl.

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:57.190
But I can keep being undefeated!

00:20:57.550 --> 00:21:00.550
That's right. Keep rising 
to the challenge, Teio!

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:01.870
Yeah!

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:05.830
I know! If I win the Tennoushou, 
come with me to karaoke again!

00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:06.840
Fair enough.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:17.370
Excuse me... Grandmother, 
have you seen the news today?

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:18.210
I have.

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:21.210
In print and on television, 
it's Teio this, Teio that...

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:24.700
I'm honestly shocked at the 
public's impression of the race.

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:28.340
I was shocked after seeing you at 
the press conference, personally.

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:33.610
I read you the tale of the tortoise 
and the hare as a child, didn't I?

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:35.000
Y-You did.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.690
Do you understand how the tortoise won?

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:42.200
The rabbit was looking at the tortoise.

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:45.110
But the tortoise was looking at the goal.

00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:48.460
Do you understand what I'm trying to say?

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:55.640
Having a rival is important.

00:21:56.420 --> 00:22:00.500
But there should be something 
more important than that.

00:22:02.370 --> 00:22:07.120
It's all right, Grandmother. I will not lose!

00:22:26.940 --> 00:22:28.040
I can do this!

00:22:28.040 --> 00:22:29.030
You can do this!

00:22:29.030 --> 00:22:30.330
I've got treats!

00:22:31.510 --> 00:22:32.000
Oh, my.

00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:34.130
Are you okay, Gold Ship-san?!

00:22:34.130 --> 00:22:37.000
The Spring Tennoushou is about to begin!
